  "body": "Refs #24\n\nAdd a caller-owned adaptive scaffold for Surface navigation. It uses the compact bar below 600 dp, the horizontal Surface bar from 600 through 839 dp, and a 96 dp leading rail from 840 dp. The page and destination IDs stay stable as the layout changes. The wide rail can scroll independently and reveal a focused destination.\n\nThe exact source tree passed 1,605 Rust tests, all three WebAssembly checks, and 18 Apple Metal offscreen tests. Two native replays returned six matching PNGs through Page.screenshot, CLI and MCP. Headless Chrome WebGPU passed 368 Material steps and 30,449 checks. The evidence includes focus, selection, composition, light and dark, RTL and 200% text.\n\n[Exact runtime evidence and source replay](https://github.com/faberline/surface/tree/b78c3bb3844e182b1cf13e6cc8db2e7ba1c84d5c/docs/evidence/md3/adaptive-navigation-scaffold-v0174-corrected-runtime)\n",
  "changed_files": 13,
